Consolidating the durable-fix track here — I'd briefly opened a parallel ticket (KS-446) before spotting this one; **KS-446 is now cancelled as a duplicate of KS-441**, and its framing + owner move are carried over below.

**Direction — give the runner more power, keep coverage intact.** The honest read is that the isolated `pr-akto` runner is simply **under-powered** for what it hosts — the full 31-service platform stack *and* the full Akto stack (dashboard + mongo + akto-testing + puppeteer) on one small box. The same scan finishes in ~21s locally but couldn't complete in ~594s there, which points at CPU/IO starvation, not the scan doing too much.

So the preferred fix is to **give the runner more grunt (bigger CPU/RAM), or split the two stacks across runners** — *not* to trim the PR scan's coverage. I'd really rather not shrink the all-endpoint BOLA/BFLA/Broken-Auth set to fit a tiny machine; that quietly weakens the security gate to solve an infra sizing problem, and the coverage is the whole point of the gate. Coverage/scope trim is a last resort, and if ever taken, flagged explicitly — never silent.

@stuart.jamieson — reassigning this to you: could you let us know whether we can **resize the "tiny machine" to something with more grunt** (more vCPU/RAM), or otherwise give the Akto stack its own runner? That's very likely the entire fix. Happy to help wire up whatever sizing/split we land on.

@kamil.kreiser — flagging for context as the KS-435 / PR #490 ceiling-raise author; the raise did its job as the unblock, this just closes out the underlying resource constraint.
